# Team Directory & Dynamic Management Implementation Plan

A comprehensive technical implementation plan for a searchable **Team Directory** page and an **Admin Dashboard Management UI** for **MessKhojo**. This system allows administrators to dynamically add, edit, and manage team members across all 10 roles (Founder, Co-Founders, CEO, CTO, CFO, COO, CMO, Founding Partner, Employees, and Interns) with live Firebase Firestore updates and fast search by **Member ID** and **Name**.

---

## Architecture Overview

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Admin Dashboard] -->|Add / Edit / Delete Member| B[(Firebase Firestore 'team_members')]
    B -->|Real-time Snapshot / Fetch| C[Public Team Directory /team]
    C -->|Fuzzy Search & Filters| D[Search Bar & Member Cards]
    D -->|Click Member| E[Member Detail Modal]
```

### 1. Data Schema (`team_members` collection in Firestore)
Each team member document in Firestore will follow this schema:

```javascript
{
  id: "MK-EXEC-001",            // Standardized Member ID (e.g. MK-FND-001, MK-CTO-001, MK-EMP-104, MK-INT-201)
  name: "Aditya Kumar Nayak",     // Full Name
  role: "Founder & CEO",        // Title / Designation
  roleCategory: "founder",      // founder | co_founder | ceo | cto | cfo | coo | cmo | founding_partner | employee | intern
  categoryLabel: "Leadership",  // Human readable group badge (Leadership, Founding Team, Core Team, Interns)
  department: "Executive & Strategy",
  email: "aditya@messkhojo.com",
  linkedin: "https://linkedin.com/in/adityanayak",
  twitter: "https://twitter.com/adityanayak",
  github: "https://github.com/adityanayak",
  bio: "Visionary leader driving the growth and digital transformation of student accommodation in Odisha.",
  avatarUrl: "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/...", // Avatar image URL or fallback UI avatar
  skills: ["Product Strategy", "Venture Growth", "Operations"],
  joinedDate: "2024-01-15",
  status: "Active",             // Active | Alumnus
  createdAt: "2026-07-23T11:00:00Z",
  updatedAt: "2026-07-23T11:00:00Z"
}
```

